{"text": "Glen Klinkhart\n\nMANAGEMENT @ PUBLIC SAFETY @ BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT\n\nLifelong Alaskan offering decade(s) of experience in Corporate Management, Public Relations, Risk\nManagement, Quality Assurance, Safety, Security, and Business development. My many years of service to\nthe public have given me the opportunity to serve my fellow Alaskans and I look forward to finding new and\nchallenging ways to continue this legacy.\n\nKnowledge and Skills\n\nOrganizational Management Policy & Procedure Development\n* Personnel and Division Development . Technology and Legal Assessments\n* Human Resources and Internal Affairs * Internal and External Communications\n. Project Tracking * Media Relations\n. Intelligence Analysis . Training/Presentations\n. Project Management * Client Needs Assessments\n* Performance Review Development * Account Management\n\nProfessional Experience\n\nDepartment of Health and Social Services (DHSS) \u2014 State of Alaska\nDirector of Drug Policy and\nProject Manager - Alaska Substance Abuse Task Force 08/2019 to Present\n\nResponsible for the oversight, management, coordination, and implementation of State of Alaska\u2019s Task Force\nresponse to the drug/opioid and alcohol abuse issues facing Alaskans, including intervention, interdiction,\ntreatment, recovery, and developing community-based wellness for all Alaskans. Working with the Office of\nthe Governor, the Alaska State Legislation, the Municipality of Anchorage, local and federal law enforcement,\npublic health, medical institutions, and the public to create and implement programs and processes to minimize\nthe affects of polysubstance misuse in Alaska.\n\nDepartment of Health and Social Services (DHSS) \u2014 State of Alaska\nExecutive/Director/Manager, Alaska Psychiatric Institute (API) 01/2019 to 08/2019",
